---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Breadcrumbs from '../components/Breadcrumbs.astro';
// The operator's real credentials are the site's entire competitive advantage —
// they must be written by the operator, not invented. Page is noindex until the
// [OPERATOR INPUT] block is replaced with the real bio.
---
<BaseLayout title="About" description="Who writes this guide." noindex={true}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: '/' }, { label: 'About' }]} />
    <article class="prose" style="margin-top: 1.2rem;">
      <h1>About this guide</h1>

      <blockquote>
        <strong>[OPERATOR INPUT — your real bio, in the first person.]</strong><br />
        This page is your credibility, so Claude left it for you. Cover: your years
        in fundraising and grant work; the specific institutions or sectors (K–12,
        higher ed, etc.) you've worked in; which of these platforms you have
        personally used or migrated; and why you started this guide. Name real
        things — that first-hand experience and your network are what make the
        recommendations trustworthy and what the rest of the site leans on.
      </blockquote>

      <p>
        The guide's premise: fundraising software should be chosen by the size of
        your shop, not by whichever vendor has the biggest ad budget. Every
        recommendation names a real constraint, every price carries a
        last-verified date, and affiliate links never decide the pick.
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
